t, then set aside.","decorations":[]}}],"paragraphData":{"textStyle":{"textAlignment":"AUTO"}}},{"type":"PARAGRAPH","id":"whgcr1294","nodes":[{"type":"TEXT","id":"","nodes":[],"textData":{"text":"Assemble the Casserole","decorations":[]}}],"paragraphData":{"textStyle":{"textAlignment":"AUTO"}}},{"type":"PARAGRAPH","id":"pjkqw1296","nodes":[{"type":"TEXT","id":"","nodes":[],"textData":{"text":"​","decorations":[]}}],"paragraphData":{"textStyle":{"textAlignment":"AUTO"}}},{"type":"PARAGRAPH","id":"k4l7j1298","nodes":[{"type":"TEXT","id":"","nodes":[],"textData":{"text":"Preheat oven to 375 degrees.","decorations":[]}}],"paragraphData":{"textStyle":{"textAlignment":"AUTO"}}},{"type":"PARAGRAPH","id":"57ebe1300","nodes":[{"type":"TEXT","id":"","nodes":[],"textData":{"text":"​","decorations":[]}}],"paragraphData":{"textStyle":{"textAlignment":"AUTO"}}},{"type":"PARAGRAPH","id":"fdiat1302","nodes":[{"type":"TEXT","id":"","nodes":[],"textData":{"text":"Lightly spay oil a casserole then spread a thin layer of mushroom sauce on the bottom. Thinly layer potatoes, chicken filling, mushroom sauce and parsnips in that order 2 times then top with the mozzarella cheese.","decorations":[]}}],"paragraphData":{"textStyle":{"textAlignment":"AUTO"}}},{"type":"PARAGRAPH","id":"x8a4w1304","nodes":[{"type":"TEXT","id":"","nodes":[],"textData":{"text":"​","decorations":[]}}],"paragraphData":{"textStyle":{"textAlignment":"AUTO"}}},{"type":"PARAGRAPH","id":"pbdc11306","nodes":[{"type":"TEXT","id":"","nodes":[],"textData":{"text":"Bake at 375 degrees 45 - 60 minutes or until golden and bubbly.","decorations":[]}}],"paragraphData":{"textStyle":{"textAlignment":"AUTO"}}},{"type":"PARAGRAPH","id":"h57q81308","nodes":[{"type":"TEXT","id":"","nodes":[],"textData":{"text":"Top with fresh chopped parsley and serve.","decorations":[]}}],"paragraphData":{"textStyle":{"textAlignment":"AUTO"}}}],"metadata":{"version":1.0,"createdTimestamp":"2023-03-08T19:16:38.174Z","updatedTimestamp":"2023-03-08T19:16:38.174Z","id":"544c32c4-dbe1-4c3f-9ebd-730673fe319c"},"documentStyle":{}},"instructions":"Make the Mushroom sauce\n\n​\n\nHeat a small sauce pot on medium heat. Add the butter and flour and cook together until bubbly to make a light roux. Add the sliced mushrooms, minced garlic and minced onion mixing them together with the roux. \n\n​\n\nI have used store bought cremini in this recipe but Chanterelles, Fried Chicken mushrooms (Lyophyllum decastes), Honey Mushrooms (Armillaria), a variety of milk caps ( Lactarius), Oyster mushrooms or Shrimp Russula (Russula xerampelina) mushrooms would be very tasty in this dish.\n\n \n\n Important Note * If using wild mushrooms for this recipe, be sure you have properly identified the mushrooms and thoroughly cleaned and cooked them before adding them to this casserole. I like to use wild mushrooms that I have already prepared, sautéed and frozen, thaw just enough to loosen them and mix them in.\n\n​\n\nAdd the skim milk, stirring constantly until it comes to a boil and begins to thicken. Remove the pot from the heat and slowly stir in the whipping cream then season with nutmeg, salt and pepper.\n\n \n\nMake the Chicken filling\n\n​\n\nHeat a skillet on medium high heat. Add cooking oil, garlic, onion and chicken. Stir-fry until the vegetables are translucent and the chicken no longer pink. Add mushroom sauce to coat, then set aside.\n\n\nAssemble the Casserole\n\n​\n\nPreheat oven to 375 degrees.\n\n​\n\nLightly spay oil a casserole then spread a thin layer of mushroom sauce on the bottom. Thinly layer potatoes, chicken filling, mushroom sauce and parsnips in that order 2 times then top with the mozzarella cheese.\n\n​\n\nBake at 375 degrees 45 - 60 minutes or until golden and bubbly.\n\nTop with fresh chopped parsley and serve.","title":"Parsnip Potato Bake with Creamy Mushroom Sauce and Chicken ","link-recipes-1-1-all":"/wild-mushrooms/"}}],"pagingMetadata":{"count":1,"offset":0,"tooManyToCount":false,"cursors":{"next":""},"has